# This repo is authored on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) and executed on a Linux
# VPS. Anything the box runs must arrive with LF endings: a shell script with
# CRLF fails on Linux with a bare "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M", and a systemd
# unit with CRLF is silently mis-parsed. Pin those explicitly rather than
# relying on each machine's autocrlf setting.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
*.timer         text eol=lf

# Python is executed on both sides; LF everywhere keeps diffs clean.
*.py            text eol=lf

# Data and docs follow the platform default.
*.md            text
*.csv           text
*.json          text
